  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, sorry the orders@ mailbox has gone missing from your Outlook. A few things to try: 1) Close Outlook completely and open it again. Shared mailboxes you have access to usually add themselves back automatically. 2) If it's still missing, sign in to Outlook on the web, right-click Folders, choose \"Add shared folder or mailbox\" and type orders@. Please let us know if it shows up there. 3) If it works on the web but not in desktop Outlook, you can add it by hand: File > Account Settings > Account Settings, double-click your account, then More Settings > Advanced > Add, and enter orders@. Please reply with what you see, especially whether orders@ opens in Outlook on the web. If it doesn't open there, your access may have been removed, and we'll pass it to our mailbox team to check with the mailbox owner. Also, your desktop is showing as offline on our side right now. If you're using it, please make sure it's connected to the network.",
  "internal_note": "User: James O'Connor (id 8), Ops Warehouse Supervisor, account active, no lockout, mailbox at 29.7% (quota is not the cause). Device BL-DT-0108 shows offline, last check-in 2026-10-09 12:53 UTC, disk fine, no warnings. Report: orders@ shared mailbox no longer shows in his Outlook folder list (it showed before). I have no tool to check shared mailbox permissions, so I could not confirm whether his access to orders@ was removed. Sent KB-011 steps (restart Outlook, test in OWA, add manually) and asked whether it opens in OWA. If OWA says he has no access, escalate to Tier 2 per KB-011/KB-006. Possible permission removal needs the mailbox owner's approval.",
